[5]
(On 2/15/03, Michael Hart wrote the following:)

A word of explanation about the series numbers.

The original idea behind the series numbers was
to encourage looking at more books, kind of a
predecessor to those little notes you get on
some sites that promote music, books, etc:

If you like this, perhaps you would like. . . ."

I just want to have SOMETHING near the top of the
book that lets people know there are more. . .just
as we encourage our readers to send suggestions for
more books for US to do. . . .

Lots of our readers start by getting one of our PG
eBooks from some other source than directly from
one of our sites or mirrors, and thus they don't
have any context of what else is available.

I'd like to at least keep the series numbers until
we can come up with something else on this order.

Also, the number doesn't have to be something exact,
it could simply say something on the order of:

At the time of publication there were over a dozen
more works listed in our catalog by this author."

I don't want these books to appear as standalones,"
but rather to encourage further reading. . . .

Michael S. Hart
<hart@pobox.com>
Project Gutenberg
Principal Instigator
"*Internet User ~#100*"

